WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:02.079
(rock music)

00:00:02.079 --> 00:00:04.470
- All right, every day I enjoy
picking out something cool

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.513
from social media to share

00:00:05.513 --> 00:00:07.200
in case you may have overlooked it.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.348
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:08.348 --> 00:00:10.680
(rock music)

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.320
Some kids just know from early on

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.510
what they're going to be in
life, what they want to be.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.790
And for me, singing was,
there was no other option.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.340
I was definitely screwed
if it wasn't singing.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.390
For a Michigan woman,

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.640
paleontology was the right choice for her.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.220
It's a decision she made
when she was seven years old

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.630
visiting the dinosaur exhibit

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.370
at the Field Museum in Chicago.

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:30.990
And recently, she celebrated

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.270
just how far she's come since then

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.850
sharing a photo of her
first trip to the museum

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:39.150
alongside a photo of her
now doing research there,

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.440
which is so incredible.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.470
We have her on the line right
now watching on WXYZ TV.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.639
Everybody say hello to Lynnea.

00:00:45.639 --> 00:00:47.618
(audience clapping)

00:00:47.618 --> 00:00:48.451
Hi.
- Hi.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.467
- Oh my God, first of all,

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.460
I love the photos next to each other.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.533
So, what was your first visit there like?

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.750
- So the first photo, I was
on a vacation to Chicago

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.870
with my parents and we
visited the Field Museum

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.280
where they had this exhibit

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.070
that was basically just this giant sandbox

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.020
that was filled with bones,

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.455
so you could go dig up your own dinosaur.

00:01:12.455 --> 00:01:15.240
And there was someone there to explain

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.430
what paleontology even is.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.020
And I think that was the first time

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.730
that I even learned what a dinosaur was.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.620
So I was like, oh my god, that's so cool.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.718
That's what I wanna be when I grow up.

00:01:24.718 --> 00:01:26.970
And then there was this station

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.710
where you could make a model of the bone.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:33.235
So my mom took this like extremely
goofy looking photo of me

00:01:33.235 --> 00:01:36.180
and that's how that happened.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.013
- I love it.

00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:38.220
So explain it like in the next picture,

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.053
like you're going back

00:01:39.053 --> 00:01:40.680
and now you're a researcher in this field

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.180
that you've wanted to
do when you were seven.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.013
That's so cool.

00:01:43.013 --> 00:01:45.270
What was that full circle moment like?

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.850
- Yeah, so I grew up

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:51.510
and then I decided that I was
gonna be a paleontologist.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.510
So, I did a master's at
University of Minnesota

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.051
and my advisor for my master's
was actually the curator

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:00.085
from the Field Museum.

00:02:00.085 --> 00:02:04.200
And he was the same guy who
helped create that exhibit

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.660
that first got me
interested in paleontology.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.150
So, everything kind of came full circle.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.760
And then we did a research visit.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.710
So, we went back to the collections

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.830
and I was thinking, this is incredible.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.290
And I showed him that goofy photo of me

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.610
and he thought it was hilarious.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:23.820
So he went and grabbed
the exact same fossil

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.310
and then he said, "Here, you
have to recreate this photo."

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:29.580
So then, I did and I posted it

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.880
and everyone else thought
it was equally goofy.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.260
- No, it's so cool.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.640
And to dream something, you know,

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.740
that's a really cool
thing to dream as a kid

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.710
and then actually for it to
come to fruition is incredible.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.117
Congratulations.

00:02:42.117 --> 00:02:43.845
- Thank you so much.
(audience clapping)

00:02:43.845 --> 00:02:45.209
- Yeah.

00:02:45.209 --> 00:02:46.230
Well, thank you so much, Lynnea,

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.243
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:50.070
And that's not all.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:51.720
Our season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.180
makers of G2, the go-to pen
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.210
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, ma'am.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.210
So they're gonna be giving
you a check for $1,000.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:01.187
How's that sound?

00:03:01.187 --> 00:03:04.182
(audience clapping)

00:03:04.182 --> 00:03:05.690
- [Lynnea] Oh my God.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:06.523
- I love it.

00:03:06.523 --> 00:03:08.309
Thank you so much, Lynnea.

00:03:08.309 --> 00:03:09.761
And you to all our guests this hour:

00:03:09.761 --> 00:03:11.762
Martha Stewart, Candace Parker,

00:03:11.762 --> 00:03:13.973
(audience clapping drowns out Kelly)

00:03:13.973 --> 00:03:16.728
Y'all have a great day, and if
it's not, try and change it.

